# No em-dashes or en-dashes anywhere

Em-dashes (`—`, U+2014) and en-dashes (`–`, U+2013) read as AI-generated,
render unpredictably in email clients and assistive tech, and break
visually on small screens. Use a plain dash (`-`) instead everywhere in
this repo: user-facing text, code comments, internal docs, and config
comments alike. Use period, comma, semicolon, or colon instead of a dash
where it reads more naturally, depending on the sentence shape.

## Where this rule applies

This is a fleet-wide, repo-wide rule. It applies to every piece of
content this repo's contributors author, not just user-facing text:

- JSX / TSX text inside components and pages
- Form validation messages and yup / zod schemas
- Toast, banner, dialog, and inline error copy
- API route response bodies - anything in `error`, `message`,
  `description`, etc.
- Email templates (subject, plain-text, HTML) - `pact-notify/internal/templates/files/*`
- Backend error strings that bubble to the UI - e.g. `status.Error`,
  `status.Errorf`, `errors.New` returned by gRPC handlers when the
  Connect code is `InvalidArgument` (pact-web surfaces these via
  `err.rawMessage`)
- Any string an end user can read
- Code comments
- Test names, `t.Skip` / `t.Errorf` messages, `describe` / `it` labels
- Makefile and shell-script echoes
- CI annotation strings (`::error::...`)
- Internal docs (`.cursor/rules/`, `.claude/`, `.agents/`, `AGENTS.md`)
  and their own descriptions / prose (not their illustrative examples -
  see below)

## Where it does NOT apply

- Generated code (`__codegen__`, `*.pb.go`, and anything else produced
  by a codegen script rather than typed by a contributor)
- Vendored/mirrored files pulled from another repo (e.g.
  `schema/**/swagger.yaml`, downloaded by `scripts/api-download.mjs`)
- Quoted external content that must stay byte-exact (e.g. a string
  copied verbatim from a third party, or fixture data a test asserts
  byte-exactly)
- This file's own illustrative before/after examples below, which
  intentionally keep the original em-dash so the diff still
  demonstrates the replacement

## Replacement guide

| Pattern | Replace with | Why |
|---|---|---|
| Sentence break: `A — B.` | `A. B.` (capitalize B) | Two thoughts -> two sentences |
| Tight aside: `X, Y — Z` | `X, Y, Z` (comma) | Aside is light enough |
| Apposition: `name — definition` | `name: definition` | Colon introduces a definition |
| Recovery instruction: `bad state — do X` | `bad state; do X` or `bad state. Do X.` | Semicolon for tight pairs |
| Plain punctuation break: `A — B` | `A - B` | Default when none of the above fit |

## Examples (from this codebase)

```diff
- Save these now — we'll only show them once.
+ Save these now. We'll only show them once.

- this is your only sign-in method — add a passkey before disconnecting
+ this is your only sign-in method; add a passkey before disconnecting

- password has appeared in a data breach — please choose a different one
+ password has appeared in a data breach. Please choose a different one

- If you didn't request a reset, ignore this message — your password hasn't changed.
+ If you didn't request a reset, ignore this message. Your password hasn't changed.
```

## Quick check before merging

```bash
# Repo-wide, excluding generated/vendored content, this should return nothing:
rg -P '[\x{2013}\x{2014}]' . \
  --glob '!src/__codegen__/**' \
  --glob '!schema/**/swagger.yaml' \
  --glob '!pnpm-lock.yaml' \
  --glob '!CHANGELOG.md'
```
